recommendation.ordinarySelftestScope:
Exactly one root-executed ordinary GREEN using the exact PROPOSED-ORDINARY-GREEN-ENVELOPE argv (eb3fa6d9…), unchanged.

Inputs:
- /input is read-only and holds exactly 2 regular 0444 files in a 0555 directory: the unchanged test (28091 B, a1c00918…) and the checker (9070 B, 4f6af890…). There must be no __pycache__, symlinks or other entries.
- /packet holds the same 20 0444 files as RED, including the original MANIFEST.json (2f91b6fc…).

Preconditions:
- a second fresh agreeing independent Opus 5.5 vote on C1-C8 and D1-D8;
- a root decision;
- root checks pins, modes and exact listings of all 22 files before the run.

Expected result:
- Ran 19, all 19 pass, 0 failures, 0 errors, exit 0;
- stdout empty;
- stderr holds only the 19 verbose 'ok' lines plus 'Ran 19 tests' and 'OK';
- the same 22 pins, modes and listings afterwards, with no new entries.

One attempt, no retry. Any deviation, including a timeout, a start failure or extra stderr, means STOP. If T01.3 fails, apply the stop rule with no tag, boundary, width or fixture refit.

A GREEN validates only the 19 tested behaviours under the shared Aiken/CPython primitive. It does not validate D2-D4. It does not cover mutants, adoption, operator, builder or native work.

